      {/* Validated input with no dropdown options */}
      <div>
        <label htmlFor="email" style={{ display: 'block', marginBottom: 6, fontWeight: 600 }}>
          Email
        </label>
        <Input
          id="email"
          options={[]}
          value={email}
          onChange={handleEmailChange}
          validate={validateEmail}
          placeholder="you@example.com"
          showAllOnEmpty={false}
        />
      </div>

      {/* Large option set – triggers virtualization */}
      <div>
        <label htmlFor="search" style={{ display: 'block', marginBottom: 6, fontWeight: 600 }}>
          Search (10,000 items)
        </label>
        <Input
          id="search"
          options={LARGE_OPTIONS}
          value={searchTerm}
          onChange={handleSearchChange}
          placeholder="Type to filter…"
          virtualizeThreshold={50}
        />
      </div>
    </div>
  );
}
```

## Key Design Decisions & Edge Cases Handled

| Concern | How it's handled |
|---|---|
| **Large option lists** | `useVirtualList` renders only the visible slice + overscan. A threshold (`virtualizeThreshold`) means small lists skip the virtualization overhead entirely. |
| **Rapid typing / performance** | `useDebounce` delays filtering by 150 ms (configurable). The filter itself uses `useMemo` so it only re-runs when the debounced value changes. |
| **No matches** | `filterOptions` returns `null` → a `useEffect` closes the dropdown automatically. |
| **Empty input** | Configurable via `showAllOnEmpty`. When `false`, the dropdown stays hidden until the user types. |
| **Keyboard navigation** | Full `ArrowUp` / `ArrowDown` / `Enter` / `Escape` / `Tab` support with wrap-around. `scrollToIndex` keeps the active item in view. |
| **Outside click** | Both a `mousedown` listener on `document` **and** a `blur` handler (with `relatedTarget` check) close the dropdown. |
| **Click vs. blur race** | Options use `onMouseDown` (not `onClick`) + `e.preventDefault()` so the input doesn't lose focus before the selection registers. |
| **Validation** | Pluggable `validate` function. Red border + `aria-invalid` + visible error message. Only runs after the user has interacted (`hasInteracted` flag). |
| **Accessibility** | Full ARIA combobox pattern: `role="combobox"`, `aria-expanded`, `aria-activedescendant`, `role="listbox"`, `role="option"`, `aria-selected`, `role="alert"` for errors. |
| **Special characters in query** | `escapeRegExp` prevents regex injection (though we use `.includes()` here, the helper is available if you switch to regex matching). |
| **Modifier keys** | `Ctrl/⌘/Alt` + key combos are ignored so copy/paste/shortcuts still work. |
| **Form submission** | `Enter` calls `e.preventDefault()` to stop the form from submitting when the dropdown is open. |
| **Disabled state** | All interaction handlers early-return when `disabled` is true. |
| **Duplicate values** | Each option is keyed by `option.value`. If your data can have duplicates, switch the key to `${option.value}-${index}`. |

Drop the `src/components/Input/` folder into your project, import `Input` from `./components/Input`, and you're ready to go. No external dependencies required.

