## Key Design Decisions

| Decision | Rationale |
|---|---|
| **MVVM** | Clean separation: View renders, ViewModel holds state, Service does I/O. |
| **`AudioRecording` protocol** | The ViewModel never touches `AVAudioRecorder` directly → fully unit-testable with a mock. |
| **`RecordingState` enum** | Exhaustive state machine; the compiler forces you to handle every case in `switch`. No impossible states. |
| **`@MainActor` on ViewModel** | All UI mutations are guaranteed on the main thread; no `DispatchQueue.main` scattered around. |
| **`@StateObject` in View** | Correct ownership: the ViewModel lives as long as the view, not recreated on re-render. |
| **Timer via Combine** | Cancellable, no manual `Timer` invalidation leaks; auto-cancels on deinit. |
| **`onDisappear` safety net** | If the user force-navigates away mid-recording, the mic is released. |
| **Equalizer as a standalone `View`** | Reusable in any screen (e.g., a mini-player). Configuration via init params. |
| **Staggered bar animation** | Each bar gets a unique `delay` + `duration` so the motion looks organic rather than mechanical. |

> **Note on `await_requestPermission`:** The synchronous bridge with a semaphore is a pragmatic compromise so the `AudioRecording` protocol stays non-`async`. In a greenfield project, prefer making the protocol `async throws` and removing the semaphore entirely.

Drop these files into your Xcode project, add the Info.plist key, and you have a fully functional, testable voice recorder with a live equalizer animation.

# Surface Character Movement (Unity 2023)

## Concept

The character raycasts to find the surface beneath it, aligns its local **up** to the hit **normal**, and projects all movement input onto the **tangent plane** of that surface. This works on cubes, spheres, and any mesh.

## Project Structure

```
Assets/
├── Scripts/
│   ├── SurfaceMovement.cs        ← main component
│   ├── SurfaceDebug.cs           ← optional visual debug
├── Scenes/
│   └── SurfaceTest.unity
```

---

## 1. `SurfaceMovement.cs`

```csharp
using UnityEngine;

[RequireComponent(typeof(CapsuleCollider))]
public class SurfaceMovement : MonoBehaviour
{
    [Header("Surface Detection")]
    [Tooltip("Distance to raycast for the surface")]
    [SerializeField] private float raycastDistance = 2f;

    [Tooltip("Layer mask for walkable surfaces")]
    [SerializeField] private LayerMask surfaceLayer = ~0;

    [Tooltip("How fast the character aligns to the surface normal (rad/s)")]
    [SerializeField] private float alignSpeed = 12f;

    [Header("Movement")]
    [SerializeField] private float moveSpeed = 5f;
    [SerializeField] private float rotationSpeed = 10f;

    [Header("Surface Offset")]
    [Tooltip("How far above the surface the character sits")]
    [SerializeField] private float surfaceOffset = 0.01f;

    // --- Runtime state ---
    private Vector3 _currentNormal = Vector3.up;
    private Quaternion _currentRotation;
    private bool _onSurface;

    private CapsuleCollider _col;
    private Rigidbody _rb;

    private void Awake()
    {
        _col = GetComponent<CapsuleCollider>();
        _rb = GetComponent<Rigidbody>();
        if (_rb == null) _rb = gameObject.AddComponent<Rigidbody>();
        _rb.isKinematic = false;
        _rb.useGravity = false;          // we handle "gravity" via the surface
        _rb.constraints = RigidbodyConstraints.None;
        _rb.collisionDetectionMode = CollisionDetectionMode.Continuous;
    }

    private void Start()
    {
        _currentRotation = transform.rotation;
    }

    private void Update()
    {
        // 1 ── Detect surface
        DetectSurface(out Vector3 hitNormal, out Vector3 hitPoint);

        if (_onSurface)
        {
            // 2 ── Align up-vector to surface normal (smooth)
            AlignToNormal(hitNormal);

            // 3 ── Move on the tangent plane
            MoveOnTangentPlane(hitNormal, hitPoint);
        }
        else
        {
            // No surface – let the character fall / stop
            _rb.velocity = Vector3.zero;
        }
    }

    // ──────────────────────────────────────────────
    //  Surface detection
    // ──────────────────────────────────────────────
    private void DetectSurface(out Vector3 normal, out Vector3 point)
    {
        normal = Vector3.up;
        point  = transform.position;
        _onSurface = false;

        // Cast from the character's feet downward along the CURRENT normal
        // (not world-down) so it works on walls, ceilings, etc.
        Vector3 origin = transform.position - _currentNormal * raycastDistance * 0.5f;
        Vector3 dir    = -_currentNormal;

        if (Physics.Raycast(origin, dir, out RaycastHit hit, raycastDistance,
                            surfaceLayer, QueryTriggerInteraction.Ignore))
        {
            normal     = hit.normal;
            point      = hit.point;
            _onSurface = true;
        }
    }

    // ──────────────────────────────────────────────
    //  Align character up → surface normal
    // ──────────────────────────────────────────────
    private void AlignToNormal(Vector3 surfaceNormal)
    {
        // Target rotation: local up == surfaceNormal, keep current heading
        Quaternion target = Quaternion.FromToRotation(
            transform.up, surfaceNormal) * transform.rotation;

        // Smooth slerp
        _currentRotation = Quaternion.Slerp(
            _currentRotation, target, alignSpeed * Time.deltaTime);

        transform.rotation = _currentRotation;

        // Lerp the stored normal so the next raycast direction eases in
        _currentNormal = Vector3.Slerp(_currentNormal, surfaceNormal,
                                       alignSpeed * Time.deltaTime);
    }

    // ──────────────────────────────────────────────
    //  Movement projected onto the tangent plane
    // ──────────────────────────────────────────────
    private void MoveOnTangentPlane(Vector3 normal, Vector3 hitPoint)
    {
        // --- Input (WASD + mouse or gamepad – adapt as needed) ---
        float h = Input.GetAxis("Horizontal");   // A / D
        float v = Input.GetAxis("Vertical");     // W / S

        // Build a local frame on the tangent plane
        Vector3 localForward = transform.forward;
        Vector3 localRight   = transform.right;

        // Project onto the plane perpendicular to the surface normal
        localForward = Vector3.ProjectOnPlane(localForward, normal).normalized;
        localRight   = Vector3.ProjectOnPlane(localRight,   normal).normalized;

        Vector3 moveDir = localForward * v + localRight * h;
        moveDir = Vector3.ProjectOnPlane(moveDir, normal).normalized; // safety

        // Apply velocity (kinematic-friendly)
        Vector3 targetVel = moveDir * moveSpeed;
        _rb.velocity = Vector3.Lerp(_rb.velocity, targetVel,
                                    rotationSpeed * Time.deltaTime);

        // --- Keep character sitting on the surface ---
        Vector3 surfacePos = hitPoint + normal * (_col.center.y + _col.radius + surfaceOffset);
        transform.position = Vector3.MoveTowards(transform.position, surfacePos,
                                                 moveSpeed * Time.deltaTime + 0.05f);
    }
}
```

