## Design notes

| CUE feature | Where it's used | Why |
|---|---|---|
| `let` bindings | `namespace`, images, ports, `nginxConf` | Single source of truth; change once, propagates everywhere |
| `#` (top-level) definitions | `#haContainer`, `#nginxContainer`, `#meta`, label shapes | Reusable, self-documenting fragments that read like a mini-schema |
| `&` (unification) | `#meta & { name: …, labels: … }` | Merge shared metadata with per-resource overrides without copy-paste |
| Label hierarchy | `#labels` → `#haLabels` / `#nginxLabels` | Adds `component` without repeating `name`/`part-of` |
| `manifests` list | Bottom of file | One evaluation target; `cue export -t` gives a clean multi-doc YAML |

The file is intentionally split into **four horizontal bands** (constants → shapes → resources → aggregate) so a reader can scan top-to-bottom and build a mental model before diving into any single resource.

