## Why This Is Efficient & Follows Best Practices

| Concern | How it's addressed |
|---|---|
| **Single round-trip to DB for nodes** | One `EntityQuery` with `accessCheck(TRUE)` + `range()` – no N+1 loads. |
| **Term lookup is O(1)** | A separate, indexed query on `taxonomy_term` (`vid` + `name`) with `range(0,1)`. In production you'd cache this via `\Drupal::cache('default')` or a config entity. |
| **Access control** | `accessCheck(TRUE)` ensures only published, viewable nodes are returned. |
| **Pagination** | `PagerManager` + `range()` keeps result sets bounded (12 per page). |
| **DI & testability** | Constructor-injected services; `create()` factory for the container. No static `\Drupal::` calls in the hot path (only `date.formatter` as a pragmatic exception). |
| **Strict types** | `declare(strict_types=1)` on every PHP file. |
| **PSR-12 / Drupal coding standards** | Final class, typed properties, docblocks on every method, `static::` in `create()`. |
| **Security** | No raw user input reaches the query; term name is a hardcoded constant. URLs are generated via `toUrl()`. |
| **Caching** | The render array is automatically cached by Drupal's render cache (page-level). For the term lookup, add a `\Drupal::cache('default')->get/set` wrapper in production. |
| **Bootstrap 5** | Card grid (`row` / `col-sm-6` / `col-lg-4`), badges, `shadow-sm`, `rounded-3`, `stretched-link`, lazy-loaded images, ARIA labels on the pager `<nav>`. |

### Optional Production Hardening

```php
// Inside resolveTermId() – add a 1-hour cache to avoid repeated term lookups:
$cache = \Drupal::cache('default');
$cid = 'article_teaser:term:foobar';
$cached = $cache->get($cid);

if ($cached) {
  return (int) $cached->data;
}

// … run the query …
$cache->set($cid, $term_id, time() + 3600);
return $term_id;
```

This keeps the hot path to **one indexed node query + one cached term lookup**, which is as lean as Drupal's query layer allows without dropping to raw SQL.

# Deluge Dark Theme + Streaming Plugin on NixOS (Pure Nix)

Since `/nix/store` is read-only, you **cannot** `sudo tar -xz` into it. Instead you create a **custom derivation** that copies the deluge package, overlays the theme, patches `index.html`, and produces a new store path. Everything below is a single NixOS module.

## 1. Create the module

Create `~/.config/nixos/deluge-theme.nix`:

```nix
{ config, pkgs, ... }:

let

  # ──────────────────────────────────────────────
  # 1. Fetch the dark-theme tarball
  # ──────────────────────────────────────────────
  # Get the hash:
  #   nix-prefetch-url https://github.com/joelacus/deluge-web-dark-theme/raw/main/deluge_web_dark_theme.tar.gz
  darkTheme = pkgs.fetchurl {
    url = "https://github.com/joelacus/deluge-web-dark-theme/raw/main/deluge_web_dark_theme.tar.gz";
    sha256 = "REPLACE_WITH_HASH";   # ← run nix-prefetch-url above
  };

  # ──────────────────────────────────────────────
  # 2. Fetch the deluge-streaming plugin
  # ──────────────────────────────────────────────
  # Get the hash:
  #   nix-prefetch-url https://github.com/JohnDoee/deluge-streaming/archive/refs/heads/main.tar.gz
  delugeStreaming = pkgs.fetchFromGitHub {
    owner = "JohnDoee";
    repo  = "deluge-streaming";
    rev   = "main";                 # pin to a commit hash for reproducibility
    hash  = "REPLACE_WITH_HASH";   # ← run nix-prefetch-url above
  };

  # ──────────────────────────────────────────────
  # 3. Build a themed copy of deluge
  # ──────────────────────────────────────────────
  themedDeluge = pkgs.stdenvNoCC.mkDerivation {
    name = "deluge-themed-${pkgs.deluge.version}";

    # We don't actually "build" anything; we copy + patch.
    dontConfigure = true;
    dontBuild     = true;
    dontFixup     = true;

    buildPhase = ''
      # Copy the entire deluge package into $out
      cp -r ${pkgs.deluge}/. $out

      # Locate the web-ui directory (Python version may vary)
      WEB_DIR=$(find "$out" -path "*/deluge/ui/web" -type d | head -1)
      if [ -z "$WEB_DIR" ]; then
        echo "ERROR: deluge/ui/web not found in ${pkgs.deluge}" >&2
        exit 1
      fi

      # Overlay the dark theme (replaces icons/ and images/)
      tar -xzf ${darkTheme} -C "$WEB_DIR/"

      # Patch index.html: insert viewport meta tag after line 19
      sed -i '19a <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1, minimum-scale=1, maximum-scale=1">' \
        "$WEB_DIR/index.html"
    '';
  };

in

{
  # ──────────────────────────────────────────────
  # 4. Replace the system deluge with the themed one
  # ──────────────────────────────────────────────
  environment.systemPackages = [
    themedDeluge
  ];

  # Make the themed deluge the one the service actually runs
  services.deluged = {
    enable = true;
    package = themedDeluge;          # ← key line
    openFirewall = true;
  };

  services.deluge-web = {
    enable = true;
    package = themedDeluge;
    openFirewall = true;
  };

  # ──────────────────────────────────────────────
  # 5. web.conf  →  set theme to "dark"
  # ──────────────────────────────────────────────
  environment.etc."deluge/.config/deluge/web.conf" = {
    user  = "deluge";
    group = "deluge";
    mode  = "0644";
    text  = ''
      {
        "theme": "dark"
      }
    '';
  };

  # ──────────────────────────────────────────────
  # 6. Install the deluge-streaming plugin
  # ──────────────────────────────────────────────
  # Deluge plugins live in  <user>/.config/deluge/Plugins/
  # We drop the fetched source tree there.
  systemd.services."deluge-plugin-streaming" = {
    description = "Install deluge-streaming plugin into deluge's Plugins dir";
    wantedBy = [ "multi-user.target" ];
    after    = [ "deluged.service" ];
    serviceConfig = {
      Type   = "oneshot";
      User   = "deluge";
      Group  = "deluge";
      ExecStart = ''
        ${pkgs.bash}/bin/bash -c '
          set -euo pipefail
          PLUGINS_DIR="/var/lib/deluge/.config/deluge/Plugins"
          mkdir -p "$PLUGINS_DIR"
          # The fetched tarball extracts to deluge-streaming-main/
          cp -r ${delugeStreaming} "$PLUGINS_DIR/deluge-streaming"
          chown -R deluge:deluge "$PLUGINS_DIR/deluge-streaming"
        '
      '';
    };
  };

  # ──────────────────────────────────────────────
  # 7. (Optional) remove any stale web.conf~ backup
  # ──────────────────────────────────────────────
  systemd.services."deluge-cleanup" = {
    description = "Remove stale web.conf~ backup";
    wantedBy = [ "multi-user.target" ];
    after    = [ "deluge-web.service" ];
    serviceConfig = {
      Type      = "oneshot";
      User      = "deluge";
      Group     = "deluge";
      RemainAfterExit = true;
      ExecStart = ''
        ${pkgs.bash}/bin/bash -c '
          rm -f /var/lib/deluge/.config/deluge/web.conf~
        '
      '';
    };
  };
}
```

## 2. Import the module

In your `configuration.nix` (or wherever you keep your NixOS modules):

```nix
imports = [
  # ... your existing imports ...
  ./deluge-theme.nix
];
```

## 3. Get the hashes (one-time)

```bash
# Dark theme tarball
nix-prefetch-url \
  https://github.com/joelacus/deluge-web-dark-theme/raw/main/deluge_web_dark_theme.tar.gz

# deluge-streaming source
nix-prefetch-url \
  https://github.com/JohnDoee/deluge-streaming/archive/refs/heads/main.tar.gz
```

Paste the printed `sha256-…` strings into the two `REPLACE_WITH_HASH` placeholders.

> **Tip:** For reproducibility, pin `rev` in `fetchFromGitHub` to an actual commit hash instead of `"main"`:
> ```bash
> git ls-remote https://github.com/JohnDoee/deluge-streaming main
> ```
> then use that 40-char SHA.

## 4. Build & switch

```bash
sudo nixos-rebuild switch
```

If you want to test just the derivation first (without touching the running system):

```bash
nix build .#themedDeluge
ls result/lib/python3.*/site-packages/deluge/ui/web/icons/   # should show dark-theme icons
```

## 5. Verify

```bash
# deluge-web should be running with the themed package
systemctl status deluge-web

# Confirm the theme is active
grep '"theme"' /var/lib/deluge/.config/deluge/web.conf
# → "theme": "dark"

# Confirm the viewport tag
grep 'viewport' /var/lib/deluge/.config/deluge/../../$(
  readlink -f /nix/store/*/deluge-themed-*/lib/python3.*/site-packages/deluge/ui/web/index.html
) | head -1

# Confirm the plugin is present
ls /var/lib/deluge/.config/deluge/Plugins/deluge-streaming/
```

Then open **http://localhost:8112** in your browser — you should see the dark theme, the viewport meta tag (no more mobile zoom issues), and the streaming plugin in the Deluge UI.

