| Original instruction | NixOS problem | Nix solution here |
|---|---|---|
| `sudo tar -xz -C /usr/lib/python3/dist-packages/…` | `/nix/store` is **read-only**; there is no `/usr/lib/python3` | `stdenvNoCC` derivation copies the package → overlays theme → outputs a **new** store path |
| `sudo nano /usr/lib/…/index.html` | Same: can't write into the store | `sed` inside the derivation's `buildPhase` |
| `nano ~/.config/deluge/web.conf` | Config must survive rebuilds | `environment.etc` declaratively manages the file |
| (no mention of plugin) | — | `fetchFromGitHub` + a `oneshot` systemd unit drops the plugin into the service user's `Plugins/` dir |

Every rebuild (`nixos-rebuild switch`) re-derives the themed package from the pristine `pkgs.deluge`, so you never fight a read-only filesystem.

