## How It Works – Step by Step

```
┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│  MOUNT                                                            │
│                                                                  │
│  1. estimateInitialCount()                                       │
│     → reads scrollContainer.clientHeight                         │
│     → divides by rowHeight (40 px)                               │
│     → e.g. 600 / 40 = 15 rows  →  fetchRows(0, 15)              │
│                                                                  │
│  2. Rows render.  Sentinel <div> sits just below the last row.   │
│                                                                  │
│  3. IntersectionObserver is created with:                        │
│       root:       the scroll container                           │
│       rootMargin: "0 0 200px 0"  ← fires 200 px before bottom   │
│       target:     the sentinel div                               │
│                                                                  │
├──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│  USER SCROLLS DOWN                                                │
│                                                                  │
│  • Sentinel enters the "root + rootMargin" zone                  │
│  • Observer callback fires → loadMore()                          │
│  • store.fetchRows(15, 15)  →  GET /api/rows?start=15&count=15  │
│  • Response appended to store.rows                               │
│  • New <tr> elements render, pushing the sentinel further down   │
│  • Observer fires again when sentinel re-enters the margin zone  │
│                                                                  │
│  • When start >= total → hasMore = false → observer is inert    │
└──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
```

### Key design decisions

| Concern | Solution |
|---|---|
| **Fixed header** | The `<thead>` lives *outside* the scroll container; the body table scrolls independently. `position: sticky` is used as a belt-and-suspenders measure if you ever restructure. |
| **Fill available space** | `estimateInitialCount()` measures the container on mount and requests just enough rows to fill it (plus a small buffer). |
| **Trigger next page** | `IntersectionObserver` with a `rootMargin` buffer of 200 px fires *before* the user hits the bottom, so loading feels seamless. |
| **Prevent duplicate fetches** | `if (this.loading) return` guard in the store action. |
| **Clean teardown** | Observer disconnected and store reset in `onBeforeUnmount`. |
| **Flexbox height** | The wrapper uses `flex-direction: column` + `min-height: 0` so the scroll container correctly constrains and scrolls within the parent's height. |

This gives you a performant, self-contained infinite table that works with any REST endpoint following the `start` / `count` pagination contract.

# Unity Geometry Shader: Pixel Extrusion

This solution uses a **point-based mesh** (one point per pixel) so the geometry shader can cleanly emit a full box per opaque pixel without duplication issues.

## Shader (`PixelExtrusion.shader`)

```hlsl
Shader "Custom/PixelExtrusion"
{
    Properties
    {
        _MainTex       ("Texture", 2D) = "white" {}
        _ExtrudeHeight ("Extrude Height", Float) = 0.5
        _PixelSize     ("Pixel Size (world units)", Float) = 0.015625
        _AlphaCutoff   ("Alpha Cutoff", Range(0, 1)) = 0.5
        _Color         ("Tint", Color) = (1, 1, 1, 1)
    }

    SubShader
    {
        Tags { "RenderType" = "Opaque" "Queue" = "Geometry" }
        Cull Back
        ZWrite On
        ZTest LEqual

        Pass
        {
            CGPROGRAM
            #pragma vertex   vert
            #pragma geometry geom
            #pragma fragment frag
            #pragma target 5.0

            #include "UnityCG.cginc"

            sampler2D _MainTex;
            float     _ExtrudeHeight;
            float     _PixelSize;
            float     _AlphaCutoff;
            float4    _Color;

            // ─── Vertex: pass-through ───────────────────────────────────
            struct AppData
            {
                float4 position : POSITION;
                float2 uv       : TEXCOORD0;
            };

            struct V2G
            {
                float4 pos   : SV_POSITION;
                float3 objPos: TEXCOORD0;   // object-space centre of the pixel
                float2 uv    : TEXCOORD1;
            };

            V2G vert(AppData v)
            {
                V2G o;
                o.pos    = UnityObjectToClipPos(v.position);
                o.objPos = v.position.xyz;
                o.uv     = v.uv;
                return o;
            }

            // ─── Geometry: one point → up to 12 triangles (a box) ──────
            struct G2F
            {
                float4 pos    : SV_POSITION;
                float3 normal : NORMAL;
                float4 color  : COLOR;
            };

            [maxvertexcount(36)]   // 6 faces × 2 tris × 3 verts
            void geom(point V2G input[1],
                      inout TriangleStream<G2F> stream)
            {
                // 1. Sample the texture at this pixel
                float4 texel = tex2D(_MainTex, input[0].uv);

                // 2. Skip transparent pixels
                if (texel.a < _AlphaCutoff)
                    return;

                // 3. Build the 8 corners of the extruded box
                float3 c  = input[0].objPos;
                float  h  = _PixelSize * 0.5;   // half-width / half-depth
                float  e  = _ExtrudeHeight;      // extrusion height (Y)

                float3 corners[8];
                //      x      y     z
                corners[0] = c + float3(-h,  0, -h);  // bottom-left-back
                corners[1] = c + float3( h,  0, -h);  // bottom-right-back
                corners[2] = c + float3( h,  0,  h);  // bottom-right-front
                corners[3] = c + float3(-h,  0,  h);  // bottom-left-front
                corners[4] = c + float3(-h,  e, -h);  // top-left-back
                corners[5] = c + float3( h,  e, -h);  // top-right-back
                corners[6] = c + float3( h,  e,  h);  // top-right-front
                corners[7] = c + float3(-h,  e,  h);  // top-left-front

                // 4. Per-face normals
                float3 normals[6];
                normals[0] = float3( 0, -1,  0);  // bottom
                normals[1] = float3( 0,  1,  0);  // top
                normals[2] = float3( 0,  0,  1);  // front  (+Z)
                normals[3] = float3( 0,  0, -1);  // back   (-Z)
                normals[4] = float3( 1,  0,  0);  // right  (+X)
                normals[5] = float3(-1,  0,  0);  // left   (-X)

                // 5. Winding-verified index lists (CCW from outside)
                //    Each face = 2 triangles = 6 indices
                int faceIdx[6][6] =
                {
                    { 0, 1, 2,  0, 2, 3 },   // bottom  (-Y)
                    { 4, 5, 6,  4, 6, 7 },   // top     (+Y)
                    { 3, 2, 6,  3, 6, 7 },   // front   (+Z)
                    { 0, 4, 5,  0, 5, 1 },   // back    (-Z)
                    { 1, 5, 6,  1, 6, 2 },   // right   (+X)
                    { 3, 7, 4,  3, 4, 0 },   // left    (-X)
                };

                // 6. Emit all 12 triangles
                for (int f = 0; f < 6; ++f)
                {
                    for (int t = 0; t < 2; ++t)
                    {
                        int i0 = faceIdx[f][t * 3 + 0];
                        int i1 = faceIdx[f][t * 3 + 1];
                        int i2 = faceIdx[f][t * 3 + 2];

                        G2F o0, o1, o2;

                        o0.pos    = UnityObjectToClipPos(float4(corners[i0], 1));
                        o0.normal = UnityObjectToWorldNormal(normals[f]);
                        o0.color  = _Color;

                        o1.pos    = UnityObjectToClipPos(float4(corners[i1], 1));
                        o1.normal = UnityObjectToWorldNormal(normals[f]);
                        o1.color  = _Color;

                        o2.pos    = UnityObjectToClipPos(float4(corners[i2], 1));
                        o2.normal = UnityObjectToWorldNormal(normals[f]);
                        o2.color  = _Color;

                        stream.Append(o0);
                        stream.Append(o1);
                        stream.Append(o2);
                    }
                }
            }

            // ─── Fragment: simple Lambert lighting ─────────────────────
            fixed4 frag(G2F i) : SV_Target
            {
                float3 lightDir = normalize(_WorldSpaceLightPos0.xyz);
                float  diff     = max(dot(normalize(i.normal), lightDir), 0.0);
                float3 col      = (0.25 + 0.75 * diff) * i.color.rgb;
                return float4(col, 1.0);
            }
            ENDCG
        }
    }
    FallBack "Diffuse"
}
```

## C# Script (`PixelExtrusionMesh.cs`)

Generates the point-cloud mesh that feeds the shader. Attach it to a `MeshFilter` + `MeshRenderer`.

```csharp
using UnityEngine;

[RequireComponent(typeof(MeshFilter), typeof(MeshRenderer))]
public class PixelExtrusionMesh : MonoBehaviour
{
    [Header("Texture")]
    [Tooltip("The alpha-mask texture. Resolution defines the grid.")]
    [SerializeField] private Texture2D maskTexture;

    [Header("Grid")]
    [SerializeField] private int resolution = 64;   // must match texture size
    [SerializeField] private float planeSize = 1f;  // world units (square)

    [Header("Shader Ref")]
    [SerializeField] private Material material;     // assign the shader above

    private void Start()
    {
        if (maskTexture == null)
        {
            Debug.LogError("Assign a mask texture in the Inspector.");
            return;
        }

        // Use the actual texture size (or override with 'resolution')
        int n = resolution;
        float px = planeSize / n;          // world-space size of one pixel
        float half = planeSize * 0.5f;

        // ── Build point mesh ──────────────────────────────────────────
        var mesh = new Mesh { name = "PixelExtrusionPoints" };
        int count = n * n;

        var verts = new Vector3[count];
        var uvs   = new Vector2[count];

        int idx = 0;
        for (int y = 0; y < n; ++y)
        {
            for (int x = 0; x < n; ++x)
            {
                // Centre of each pixel in object space (Y = 0 plane)
                float ox = -half + (x + 0.5f) * px;
                float oz = -half + (y + 0.5f) * px;
                verts[idx] = new Vector3(ox, 0f, oz);

                // UV pointing to the centre of the texel
                uvs[idx] = new Vector2((x + 0.5f) / n, (y + 0.5f) / n);

                ++idx;
            }
        }

        mesh.vertices = verts;
        mesh.SetUVs(0, uvs);
        mesh.SetIndices(new int[0], MeshTopology.Point, 0); // no indices for points
        mesh.RecalculateBounds();

        GetComponent<MeshFilter>().sharedMesh = mesh;

        // ── Set shader parameters ─────────────────────────────────────
        if (material != null)
        {
            material.mainTexture     = maskTexture;
            material.SetFloat("_PixelSize", px);
        }
        GetComponent<MeshRenderer>().sharedMaterial = material;
    }
}
```

## How It Works

```
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│  INPUT MESH (N×N points on a Y=0 plane)                        │
│                                                                 │
│  •  p00  p01  p02  …  p0N                                      │
│  •  p10  p11  p12  …  p1N        ← one point per texel         │
│  •  p20  p21  p22  …  p2N         UV = centre of texel         │
│  •  …   …   …   …   …                                               │
│  •  pN0  pN1  pN2  …  pNN                                      │
└──────────────────────────┬──────────────────────────────────────┘
                           │  vertex shader (pass-through)
                           ▼
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│  GEOMETRY SHADER  (per point)                                   │
│                                                                 │
│  1. tex2D(_MainTex, uv)  →  sample the pixel                   │
│  2. if (alpha < cutoff)  →  emit nothing (skip)                │
│  3. else                 →  emit a 12-triangle box             │
│                            • base  at  y = 0                   │
│                            • top   at  y = _ExtrudeHeight      │
│                            • width/depth = _PixelSize          │
│                            • 6 faces × 2 tris = 36 verts       │
└──────────────────────────┬──────────────────────────────────────┘
                           │
                           ▼
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│  FRAGMENT SHADER                                                │
│  Simple Lambert:  ambient 0.25 + diffuse 0.75 × dot(N, L)      │
└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
```

