| **2** | Assign your alpha-mask texture (e.g. a logo with transparency) to **Main Texture**. |
| **3** | Set **Pixel Size** to `planeSize / textureResolution` (e.g. `1/64 ≈ 0.015625`). |
| **4** | Set **Extrude Height** to the desired block height in world units. |
| **5** | Create an empty GameObject, add `PixelExtrusionMesh`, assign the material and the texture. |
| **6** | Make sure the texture's **Filter Mode** is **Point (no filter)** so the geometry shader samples exact texels. |

### Performance note
A 64×64 texture produces 4 096 points; every opaque pixel emits 36 vertices (12 triangles). A 256×256 texture with 50 % coverage would emit ~983 k triangles in a single draw call—fine for a hero object, but consider LOD or a lower-res mask for large scenes. The `[maxvertexcount(36)]` bound is tight, so the driver can allocate the stream efficiently.

